<title>USA: Maine, New Hampshire regulators ok LNG project.</title>
<headline>Maine, New Hampshire regulators ok LNG project.</headline>
<dateline>PORTLAND, Maine 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Public utility commissions in Maine and New Hampshire approved a contract between Granite State Gas Transmission Inc and its affiliate, Northern Utilities Inc, for an LNG facility, the firms said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The 20-year contract for natural gas storage and vaporization services from Granite State's proposed 580,000 barrel (2Bcf) LNG project will be located in Wells, Maine.</p>
<p>Granite State Gas Transmission Inc is a subsidiary of Bay State Gas Co.</p>
</text>
